    <briefdescription>
<para>Helpers for bounded shutdown joins on cooperative worker threads. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>These helpers are intended for shutdown paths that already requested worker cancellation (for example by toggling an atomic stop flag and notifying a condition variable). They bound the caller&apos;s wait so teardown cannot block forever if a worker becomes stuck while still allowing the underlying thread to be joined asynchronously by a detached watcher. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
